<task id="133" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>C11 — secure provisioning can no longer lock the creator out: share before the owner move, verify the share survived, compensate on failure, and make a partially-provisioned record resumable instead of 409 — while a genuinely provisioned record still gets 409 already_provisioned</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (authored 2026-09-30, session 27; defect C11)</phase>
    <gate>after-144 (task 144 rewrites Step 3 of the same endpoint to a named non-default owner team and generalizes provisioning to sprk_matter and sprk_workassignment; this task's fix must cover every root type provisioning handles once 144 lands)</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <status-note>**Round c1, 2026-10-03.** Escalation trigger 4 (Assign cascade under compensation) is ANSWERED by owner round 10 item 4 ((c) then (a)) and implemented: ONE reusable primitive, AssignCascadeChildOwners, snapshots each cascaded child's own owner before any write and restores it after a verified undo (task 148 reuses it). Owner round 10 item 5 decided the kept-container question (note 14.3): as shipped. No escalation trigger is open. NOT closed by this executor (main session): the manual live gate (a)-(j) and the sprk_createdbyperson schema apply before master (both approved by owner round 11 for the main session at integration); publish size; and whether round 11's blanket approval of the batch-4 live steps covers REPLAY as the (e) method (raised verifier round 1 item 9) - if the main session reads it as not covered, it asks the owner before running (e). Full record: notes/task-133-provision-creator-lockout.md section 16. **Round c1-r1, 2026-10-03 (verifier on c1).** The two child-restore outcomes c1 left untested - a child whose owner cannot be read before its restore (Unreadable) or read back after it (Unverified) - are pinned as cascade_children_not_restored with the outcome, nextCall and CRITICAL line (owner round 10 item 4); seeds S19-S22 bite. Comment wording: the kept-container decision (round 10 item 5) and what Gone means. Recorded for the live gate and task 148: the sharepointdocument behaviour in an integration-on org is unproven (fails closed either way). The NOT-closed list above is unchanged. Note section 17. **Round c1-r2, 2026-10-03 (verifier on c1-r1; owner round 13).** The last unpinned child-restore failure is pinned: a child PATCH Dataverse accepts but does not apply (NotApplied) is named in cascade_children_not_restored, never counted restored (seed V3 bites). Also pinned: the snapshot refuses a row read without an id (V18), and a resume or a work assignment reads no cascaded rows (V17, R1). A 401/403 on the snapshot read is now Refused (deterministic: an administrator checks the BFF application user's Read privilege), not a retry that fails every time. OWNER ROUND 13 ITEM 2 (BINDING) answers the (e) question above: gate (e), the compensation replay on a throwaway TEST project, is COVERED by round 11's approval; it stays a main-session live step, run with the rest of the live gate at integration. Owner round 13 item 1 (for task 148: unsecure re-owns the location rows by the task-146 non-secure-child rule) is recorded in note 16.2. Still NOT closed (main session): publish size; the manual live gate (a)-(j) and the sprk_createdbyperson schema dry run / -Apply / -Verify before master (owner round 11). Note section 18. **Round c1-r3, 2026-10-03 (verifier on c1-r2; branch task/uac-r2-133-c1-r3 - the instructed name task/uac-r2-133-c1-r1 already exists as round c1-r1).** The verifier found no executor code fix remaining. Its one minor item is closed: the wizard's copy for cascade_children_unreadable with cascadeChildState refused now names "the service's permission to read them" beside the records, as the server detail and guide 7a do since 401/403 became refused (seed CL5 bites). No C# changed. Still NOT closed (main session): publish size (the measurement before merge, note 19.4); the manual live gate (a)-(j) and the sprk_createdbyperson schema dry run / -Apply / -Verify (owner round 11; (e) by replay covered by owner round 13 item 2); Step 9 (TASK-INDEX.md status cell). Note section 19. **Round c1-r4, 2026-10-03 (verifier on c1-r3; branch task/uac-r2-133-c1-r3.-r2, the instructed name).** The last unpinned restore rule is pinned: a cascaded child whose row no longer reads back after its owner bind is named in cascade_children_not_restored as NotApplied (bind accepted) or Refused (bind refused), never counted restored (fixture RemoveChildOnBindFor; seeds S13 and S16, fail-open survivors, now bite). OWNER ROUND 14 ITEM 3 (BINDING; relayed mid-round by the main session, corroborated on the work branch at 9d88da386) is implemented: container_ownership_unreadable (new extension containerOwnershipState) and resume_creator_unavailable (new creatorState refused) classify a read Dataverse refuses (401/403, and a 400, by the cascade reads' one rule AssignCascadeChildOwners.IsRefusedRead) as an administrator's job, not a retry; 503/429 stay retryable; the wizard's copy for each is non-retryable; guide 7a updated (note 20.7; seeds K1-K10 and CL6-CL10 bite). Publish size: the c1-r3 verifier's measurement is now recorded (note 20.3): 45.66 MB to 45.69 MB, +0.04 MB, Compress-Archive Optimal, 212 = 212 files, against the work-branch merge base 6b243f092, for 3062d960f; round 14's small C# change is not re-measured (the main session measures the final head); no package changed. Recorded for the main session and task 148, not changed: the child bind's PATCH has no If-Match, so it can upsert a row deleted mid-restore (LOW, note 20.2). Still NOT closed (main session): the manual live gate (a)-(j) and the sprk_createdbyperson schema dry run / -Apply / -Verify (owner round 11; (e) by replay covered by owner round 13 item 2); Step 9 (TASK-INDEX.md status cell). Note section 20.</status-note>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Authorization-boundary .cs change (tags bff-api, auth, security) that reorders mutations on the secure-record isolation path and changes the idempotency contract of a live endpoint.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security isolation boundary: the fix trades between "locked box" (fail closed, unusable) and "back in the creator's BU" (usable, not isolated) on every failure branch, and must keep the 409 idempotency guarantee intact for completed provisions. Requires judgment on Dataverse share/assign semantics that must be proven live.</model-tier-reason>
