  <escalation>
    <trigger>`organization.sharetopreviousowneronassign` is true in dev: STOP. Every assign (including compensation) would then add a platform-issued share, and the post-move read-back would see a share this code did not grant. Present the setting and its effect per CLAUDE.md §6 (task 144 carries the same stop).</trigger>
    <trigger>Any creation path of a provisionable root (wizard host, SummarizeFilesDialog, or a BFF/Office/Assistant server-side create after task 144 widens provisioning to matters and work assignments) creates the row through an application identity (so `createdby` is an application user): `createdby` cannot be the persisted creator for those rows. STOP and bring the choice (a new server-stamped creator column with a CLAUDE.md §11 justification, `createdonbehalfby`, or another existing column) to the owner, with a recommendation, rather than sharing on resume to whoever calls. Recommendation to carry: the existing `createdby` for human-created rows plus refusal (own reasonCode) for app-created rows, until the owner decides.</trigger>
    <trigger>The live census finds a secure-team-owned row whose `sprk_containerid` is non-empty but is NOT a container provisioning created (e.g. a pre-task-076 business-unit cascade value), OR finds any create-time writer of `sprk_containerid` on a provisionable root (e.g. an active field-mapping rule): the "team-owned + container recorded = provisioned" marker would 409 such a row forever. STOP and list the rows/rules; do not widen the resume condition on a guess.</trigger>
    <trigger>Any provisionable root's 1:N relationship cascades Assign (background (d)): the forward move and the compensating move would re-own children, and compensation cannot restore each child's own previous owner. STOP and present per CLAUDE.md §6 — options: (a) snapshot and restore each re-owned child's owner in compensation; (b) no compensation for that root type (resume only); (c) coordinate with task 148, which owns child ownership at provisioning. Recommendation: (c) then (a). ANSWERED 2026-10-03 (owner round 10 item 4, BINDING): "coordinate with task 148's child-ownership logic, then snapshot and restore each re-owned child's own owner (options (c) then (a))" - implemented in round c1 (note section 16).</trigger>
    <trigger>The live proof shows neither share-first nor an immediate post-move grant can be made reliable (e.g. GrantAccess on a team-owned secure record is refused for the app user): the design premise fails — STOP and escalate with the evidence.</trigger>
