  <amendments>
    <amendment n="R3" date="2026-09-30" source="owner round 3 (session27 note) — BINDING">(S5 invariant, owner round 3) A secure record must ALWAYS keep at least one person who can see it — provisioning must never leave a secure record with nobody able to open it; this is the invariant this task's share-first + verified compensation + resume design exists to guarantee. Add an explicit acceptance check that after every outcome (success, compensated failure, resume) at least one human holds access.</amendment>
    <amendment n="R10" date="2026-10-03" source="owner round 10 items 4 and 5 (session27 note) — BINDING">(Item 4) Compensation's reverse Assign cascade: snapshot each child the Assign cascade re-owns (team, sharepointdocumentlocation, sharepointdocument) with its own current owner before the forward move, and after a compensating reverse move restore each child to its snapshotted owner; fail closed and report — a child whose restore fails is named in the response and in a CRITICAL log, with the next call to make; ONE reusable primitive that task 148 reuses for transitions (implemented as AssignCascadeChildOwners, round c1). Acceptance added: the restore after compensation puts every child back on its own pre-call owner, including a child whose owner differed from the root's; a seed that skips the restore fails. (Item 5) A record that keeps its own container and fails after its move stays AS SHIPPED: no automatic resume; the response names the Manage Access recovery (note 14.3, option C).</amendment>
    <amendment n="R14" date="2026-10-03" source="owner round 14 item 3 (session27 note) — BINDING">container_ownership_unreadable and resume_creator_unavailable (creatorState unreadable) classify 401/403 as Refused (an administrator must act), as the cascade reads already do; 503/429 stay retryable. Implemented in round c1-r4 (note 20.7): one rule (AssignCascadeChildOwners.IsRefusedRead, 400/401/403), containerOwnershipState and creatorState refused, non-retryable client copy, guide 7a; acceptance: 401 and 403 each Refused and not offered as a retry, 503/429 still retryable, each pinned by tests that seeds K1-K10 and CL6-CL10 prove bite.</amendment>
  </amendments>
</task>
